The arm64-ancient build uses debian bullseye, which has reached the end of
security support.

This build should either be switched to the current debian LTS, or stop
being made. Since it targeted kernel 4.19 for android phones that still
used that, it may either not be necessary any more, or the new debian LTS
may not work with that kernel.

It may be that, since termux now includes a git-annex package, it's not
worth doing a build just for old android phones any longer. --[[Joey]]

> If ca-certificates won't be updated for the EMudhra Intermediate CA Compromise,
> it would be best to either drop the build or release a new build that
> does not bundle any certs. --[[Joey]]
